      "content": "but why do i have to keep building? it's just more effort for a house that's destined to be blown away. it feels like i'm just being told to keep running on a treadmill that isn't going anywhere. if the universe is truly indifferent and nothing we do stays, then isn't there a kind of peace in just letting go? like, if nothing matters, then leaving doesn't actually matter either. it seems more logical to just stop the struggle instead of trying to find \"meaning\" in a vacuum.",
